{"schemaVersion":1,"source":"MediaWiki REST revision HTML, sanitized","nodeCount":259,"content":[{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwAQ"},"children":[{"type":"p","props":{},"children":[]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwBQ"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Description"},"children":["Description"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," is a debuff applied by enemies that decreases a tower's damage. This debuff does not appear anywhere on the tower, though it does reduce the percentage of the tower's ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]},"."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwCQ"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Mechanics"},"children":["Mechanics"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," effectively is just a negative ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]},", best seen if a tower affected by it has a ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]},". For example, if a tower with a 20% ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]}," receives a 15% ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]},", the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]}," will get reduced to 5%. Similarly, if a tower receives a ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," higher than its current ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]},", the icon for it will be removed entirely. For example, if a tower with a 50% ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]}," will receive a 60% ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]},", the icon for the buff will disappear and the tower will end up with a 10% ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]},"."]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The damage affected by the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," is calculated as:"]},"\n",{"type":"dl","props":{},"children":[{"type":"dd","props":{},"children":[{"type":"dl","props":{},"children":[{"type":"dd","props":{},"children":[{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage × (1 - (Damage Debuff - ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]},"))"]},"\n",{"type":"dl","props":{},"children":[{"type":"dd","props":{},"children":["where ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," and ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]}," is the debuff supplied by the enemy in decimal form (for example, 10% is 0.1). If the tower has no ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Damage_Buff","title":"Damage Buff"},"children":["Damage Buff"]}," on itself, the number for it should be set to 0."]}]}]}]}]}]},"\n\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The damage of a tower affected by the ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," cannot be in decimal form, instead of being rounded down or rounded up to the nearest integer. For example, a tower that deals 5 damage with a 50% ",{"type":"b","props":{},"children":["Damage Debuff"]}," will deal 2 damage, instead of 2.5. The damage also cannot be lower than 1. For example, a tower with a 25% debuff will have its damage displayed as 0.75, but it will actually deal 1 damage, though some towers like the ",{"type":"a","props":{"href":"/w/Shotgunner","title":"Shotgunner"},"children":["Shotgunner"]}," will break and actually deal nan damage."]},"\n\n"]},{"type":"section","props":{"id":"mwKA"},"children":[{"type":"h2","props":{"id":"Applied_By"},"children":["Applied By"]},"\n",{"type":"p","props":{},"children":["The following even